    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Detachment" hidden="false" id="4599-af3d-f084-7678">
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Detachements" id="29b2-3011-f856-2c4a" hidden="false">
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Beasts of Lustria" hidden="false" id="6075-c5ca-e09f-8338" sortIndex="2">
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="ad08-4a98-917e-7bcf" includeChildSelections="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Primal Rage" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities" hidden="false" id="57af-5c78-6ee7-e332">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">If a **Monster** or **Beast** unit made an attack with a **Companion** weapon, place a rage token next to it to a maximum of 3. If this unit did not attack with a **Companion** weapon this turn, remove all rage tokens it has.

Add 1 to the Attacks characteristic of this unit’s Companion weapons for each rage token it has until the end of the next turn.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Protection of Quetzl" hidden="false" id="d6d3-9a8e-3a94-26ec" sortIndex="1">
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="c636-8455-9f12-eb7e" includeChildSelections="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Divine Defence" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities" hidden="false" id="723f-70e9-418e-e9d9">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">Friendly **Saurus** **Infantry** units gain +1 to their toughness characteristic and +1 to strength of their melee weapons.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Seers of Tepok" hidden="false" id="ec63-9443-40ea-2bd3" sortIndex="3">
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="9ddb-a879-9eb2-90df" includeChildSelections="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Warp Conduit" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities" hidden="false" id="df4e-1fb8-1fea-ac88">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">Once per Command Phase a **Psyker** or **Saurus Astrolith Bearer** unit of your choice can enter the Channeling Stance, that unit is now considered the Channeling unit.
While in Channeling Stance that unit can&apos;t make a Charge or Advance move, its movement characteristic is reduced by 2&quot; and is not eligible to make an attack in its Shooting and Fight Phase. While a **Psyker** unit is within 3&quot; of a Channeling Unit, its **Psychic** Weapons have +1 to hit and wound rolls as well as **Ignores Cover**.
Only one unit can benefit from this ability per Channeling unit in range.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Mounts of Itzl" hidden="false" id="4cd9-8afc-78fb-0b6d" sortIndex="4">
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="3533-3ae7-ac28-7dad" includeChildSelections="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Frienzied Riders" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities" hidden="false" id="ee3e-08aa-5f9d-f75a">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">**Mounted** units can Charge in the same turn they advanced, in addition in a **Mounted** unit charged this turn its melee weapons gain +1 to their attacks characteristic.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Spawns of Sotek" hidden="false" id="8559-679d-f3ad-7c6b" sortIndex="5">
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="c971-e097-3dc1-1a40" includeChildSelections="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Children of The Serpent" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities" hidden="false" id="43f8-7c96-9112-1e44">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">If a **Kroxigor** unit and a **Skink** **Infantry** unit are within 6&quot; of each other, the **Skink** **Infantry** unit gains +2 toughness characteristic while the **Kroxigor** unit gains +3&quot; to its movement characteristic.
The **Bastildon With Ark of Sotek** is counted as both a **Skink** **Infantry** and a **Kroxigor** unit by this ability.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Wings of Chotec" hidden="false" id="7788-9ca3-731f-ea19" sortIndex="6">
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="2fde-d200-aa35-4066" includeChildSelections="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Winged Hunters" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities" hidden="false" id="d691-b19c-4b0b-faa7">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">At the begining of your every command phase pick one of the following abilities, this ability will remain in effect until the next ability is picked.

**Air Maneuvers**: The **Attack From On High** ability now also gives the benefit of **Stealth** if the conditions are met.
**Extra Cargo**: **Terradon Chief**, **Terradon Raiders** and **Terradon Raiders With Fireleech Bolas** can pick 2 targets for their **Deadly Cargo** ability instead of 1.
**Agile Beasts**: Attacks targeting **Ripperdactyl Raiders** or **Ripperdactyl Chief** units suffer a -1 penalty to their wound rolls if that unit has fallen back this turn. These units also automatically succeed desperate escape tests.


No matter the ability picked all Non **Slann** **Fly** units gain the **Swift and Nimble** Ability.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <infoLinks>
                <infoLink name="Swift and Nimble" id="454b-10ad-a8e3-12be" hidden="false" type="profile" targetId="7fd4-770d-0107-e487"/>
              </infoLinks>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="07c6-64b1-6b82-8990" includeChildSelections="false"/>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="3bed-69af-910d-291a" includeChildSelections="false"/>
          </constraints>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
      <constraints>
