  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="The Great Plan" id="31b9-5664-d133-3668" hidden="false">
      <description>If your Army Faction is **Seraphon**, at the the start of your deployment phase, pick one of the following Asterism abilities:



**Itzl, The Tamer**: Weapons used by friendly **Seraphon** **Beast** and **Monster** units have **Sustained Hits** 2.

**Quetzl, The Preserver**: Subtract 1 from the AP characteristic of melee weapons for attacks that target friendly **Seraphon** units that are wholly within your deployment zone. If you control more Objective Points in No Man&apos;s Land than your opponent, No Man&apos;s Land counts as friendly territory.

**Sotek, The Deliverer**: Add 2&quot; to the Move characteristic of friendly **Seraphon** units, **Skink** units also don&apos;t need to spend extra movement when moving verticaly or through difficult terrain.

**Tepok, The Seer**: Add 1 to Wound rolls and Attacks characteristic for friendly **Seraphon** **Psyker** units.

**Chotec, The Invigorator**: In your command phase pick a unit below its starting strength and restore 2 lost wound to it, at the begining of your enemies command phase restore another 2 lost wounds to the same unit.


At the start of the third battle round, if you meet the condition below that corresponds to the Asterism you picked in the deployment phase you may pick one additional Asterism ability. That ability can be used in addition to the one you picked in the deployment phase.


**Itzl, The Tamer**: 2 or more enemy units have been destroyed.

**Quetzl, The Preserver**: There are more friendly units than enemy units wholly within friendly territory.

**Sotek, The Deliverer**: The enemy Warlord is within engagment range of one of your units or has been destroyed.

**Tepok, The Seer**: There is at least one friendly **Psyker** unit not within engagment range of an enemy unit on the battlefield and no friendly **Psyker** units have been destroyed this combat.


**Chotec, The Invigorator**: No Character unit in your army is below half strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Companion" id="22c2-1752-d282-939d" hidden="false">
      <description>Weapons with [Companion] in their profile are known as Companion weapons. If a Companion weapon attack is made it is considered to be made by this units mount or a tamed **Beast**/**Monster**. If a Companion weapon or ability causes any unit to suffer one or more wounds, each of those wounds is considered to have been inflicted by a Companion Attack.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
